<title>PORTUGAL: Banks issue 1.6 bln esc in EDP indexed bonds.</title>
<headline>Banks issue 1.6 bln esc in EDP indexed bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's Banco de Comercio e Industria (BCI) and Banco Santander de Negocios Portugal (BSNP) said they had issued 1.6 billion escudos of three-year bonds indexed to the share price of EDP-Electricidade de Portugal.</p>
<p>The bonds will pay interest equal to 150 percent of the average quarterly gain in price of EDP shares, with 80 percent of invested capital guaranteed, the banks' joint statement said.</p>
<p>Subscriptions close on July 18th.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-353-8254</p>
</text>
